# ==========================================================================
# Zinga's Assistant: baked ~/.hermes/.env (NON-SECRET defaults only)
# ==========================================================================
# Adapted from Nick's Stack (MIT). No keys, tokens, phone numbers or customer
# data ever go in this file. Real secrets live in the 1Password vault
# "Zingas Assistant", Secure Note "Assistant Secrets" (one field per name below).

OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=/root/Documents/ZingasVault
WIKI_PATH=/root/Documents/ZingasVault
TERMINAL_TIMEOUT=60
TERMINAL_LIFETIME_SECONDS=300
ASSISTANT_TIME_ZONE=America/Indiana/Indianapolis

# ==========================================================================
# Key contract: field names in 1Password. Names only; NEVER commit values.
# ==========================================================================
# For the agent (Hermes):
#   OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN   1Password service account (goes in ~/.hermes/.op.env)
#   (Not in 1Password: TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS and
#   TELEGRAM_HOME_CHANNEL are set by Orgo's Telegram pairing in ~/.hermes/.env,
#   and the AI is a Nous Portal sign-in, so there is no model key.)
#   SUPABASE_URL               dashboard's Supabase project (assistant schema)
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  server-only key for the same project
#   SF_LOGIN_URL               Salesforce Connected App (write-scoped; ON HOLD, leave empty)
#   SF_CLIENT_ID
#   SF_CLIENT_SECRET
#   ESTIMATOR_URL              e.g. https://zingas-estimator.vercel.app
#   ESTIMATOR_SERVICE_TOKEN    read-only assistant API on the Estimator
#   HEALTHCHECKS_PING_URL      dead-man ping, every 10 minutes
#
# For quo-bridge ONLY: 1Password vault "Zingas Bridge", Secure Note "Bridge
# Secrets", read by its own service account. Never given to the agent, and the
# agent's service account cannot read that vault, so the agent has no way to
# text a customer by itself:
#   QUO_API_KEY                Quo API key
#   QUO_PHONE_NUMBER_ID        the business number's Quo id
#   QUO_WEBHOOK_SECRET         verifies webhooks really come from Quo
#   APPROVALS_BOT_TOKEN        second Telegram bot that carries Approve/Edit/Skip
#   APPROVER_TELEGRAM_ID       the only Telegram user who can approve
#   GERRIT_CELL                E.164, for the 10-minute escalation text
#   COMPOSIO_API_KEY           Composio project key, for mail-bridge only. mail-bridge
#                              opens a Composio session limited to read mail, search
#                              mail, create draft and read calendar, and is the only
#                              thing Val talks to for Gmail. Val never holds this key,
#                              so she cannot unlock send, forward or delete.
